    "result_text": "The full suite is green. \n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `displayName` field on owner responses, formatted as `LastName, FirstName`.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a read-only `displayName` string property to the `Owner` schema (alongside `id` and `pets`). This regenerates `OwnerDto` with a `displayName` getter/setter.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added a MapStruct mapping expression on `toOwnerDto(Owner)`:\n   ```java\n   @Mapping(target = \"displayName\",\n       expression = \"java(owner.getLastName() + \\\", \\\" + owner.getFirstName())\")\n   ```\n\nSince it's a derived response field, no change was needed in the OfficeFloor endpoint pipeline \u2014 the existing `RespondWithOwnerCreated` / GET responder already maps the entity through `OwnerMapper`, so both the create and read paths now expose `displayName` from the stored names.\n\nThe acceptance test `coreComputesDisplayName` and the full suite pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`).",
